       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The maximum labeled daily dose for adults is 3200 mg/day, so this is double that. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is 3200 mg/day, the maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours.** This is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day, divided.** For example, 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then add it in a note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
